  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Cgi Federal has $1.3B in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Cgi Federal won 300 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.4M. Cgi Federal's obligations are up 11.1% year over year. Cgi Federal's FY21 obligations were $1B. Cgi Federal's FY22 obligations were $1.1B. Cgi Federal's FY23 obligations were $1.1B. Cgi Federal's FY24 obligations were $1.2B. Cgi Federal's FY25 obligations were $1.2B. General Services Administration bought $268M from Cgi Federal and Department of State bought $267M. Other Computer Related Services is the largest market for Cgi Federal with $569M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services with $287M and Computer Facilities Management Services with $218M. Cgi Federal also does work in Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services with $69.1M and Facilities Support Services with $66M. This profile reports contract obligations, and award-value totals in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values when present. Current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Cgi Federal's top buying agencies?",
        "body": "General Services Administration bought $268M from Cgi Federal. Department of State bought $267M and Department of Justice bought $154M. Department of Veterans Affairs bought $136M and Social Security Administration bought $129M. Department of Homeland Security bought $78M and Department of Health and Human Services bought $77.3M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services does Cgi Federal sell to government buyers?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is Cgi Federal's largest market at $569M. Computer Systems Design Services is the second-largest market at $287M and Computer Facilities Management Services is the third at $218M. Cgi Federal also sells Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $69.1M, Facilities Support Services at $66M, and Custom Computer Programming Services at $50.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
